## The five-houses puzzle (world conventions, lib/world2, no environment)
##
## Original English:
##   There are five houses in a row, numbered 1 to 5 from left to right. Each house is painted a
##   different color. In each house lives a person of a different nationality. Each of the five
##   owners drinks a certain beverage, smokes a certain brand of cigar, and keeps a certain pet.
##   No two owners have the same pet, smoke the same cigar, drink the same beverage, or share a
##   nationality. Questions: 1. Who drinks water? 2. Who owns the zebra?
##   Clues: 1 There are exactly five houses. 2 The Englishman lives in the red house. 3 The Swede
##   keeps dogs as pets. 4 The Dane drinks tea. 5 The green house is immediately to the left of
##   the white house. 6 The green house's owner drinks coffee. 7 The person who smokes Pall Mall
##   rears birds. 8 The owner of the yellow house smokes Dunhill. 9 The man living in the center
##   house (House 3) drinks milk. 10 The Norwegian lives in the first house (House 1). 11 The man
##   who smokes Blends lives next to the one who keeps cats. 12 The man who keeps horses lives
##   next to the man who smokes Dunhill. 13 The owner who smokes BlueMaster drinks beer. 14 The
##   German smokes Prince. 15 The Norwegian lives next to the blue house.
##   Show the elimination matrix or deductions; answer who drinks water and who owns the zebra.
##
## Encoding:
##   World: house-1..5 (^position, ^left/^right neighbour handles, ^candidate for every value
##   still possible), the 25 values (^group: their category; selection-world's look-ahead copy
##   does not copy an attribute named ^category), the 5 categories, the clues as data
##   (relation same | position | left-of | next-to), and the puzzle (desired: ^solved true).
##   Reasoning is candidate elimination (the elimination matrix). Task operator eliminate removes
##   one candidate for a stated reason: a clue, a naked single (a house has one value left in a
##   category) or a hidden single (a value has one house left). When no elimination applies, the
##   agent prints the matrix and branches on the first open cell (task operator assign); the
##   branches tie and look-ahead (selection-world, iterative deepening) settles the tie: a branch
##   that empties a cell or a value is a failure, one that solves the puzzle a success.
##   Clue 1 is the structure itself (five houses).

## Propose initialize-zebra when its conditions below hold.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute object 50

sp {zebra*propose*initialize-zebra
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-zebra ^task-operator false)
}

## propose*initialize-agent-world tests only -^name, so it stays proposed after it has built
## ^world; reject it once ^world exists (library finding).
sp {zebra*reject*initialize-agent-world*world-exists
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> ^operator <o> +)
   (<o> ^name initialize-agent-world)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> -)
}

## Apply initialize-zebra.
sp {zebra*apply*initialize-zebra
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-zebra ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name zebra ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <puzzle> <h1> <h2> <h3> <h4> <h5> <c-color> <v-red> <v-green> <v-white> <v-yellow> <v-blue> <c-nationality> <v-English> <v-Swede> <v-Dane> <v-Norwegian> <v-German> <c-drink> <v-tea> <v-coffee> <v-milk> <v-beer> <v-water> <c-smoke> <v-PallMall> <v-Dunhill> <v-Blends> <v-BlueMaster> <v-Prince> <c-pet> <v-dogs> <v-birds> <v-cats> <v-horses> <v-zebra> <k2> <k3> <k4> <k5> <k6> <k7> <k8> <k9> <k10> <k11> <k12> <k13> <k14> <k15>)
   (<puzzle> ^object-handle puzzle ^anchored true ^type puzzle)
   (<h1> ^object-handle house-1 ^anchored true ^type house ^position 1 ^right house-2
           ^candidate |red| |green| |white| |yellow| |blue| |English| |Swede| |Dane| |Norwegian| |German| |tea| |coffee| |milk| |beer| |water| |PallMall| |Dunhill| |Blends| |BlueMaster| |Prince| |dogs| |birds| |cats| |horses| |zebra|)
   (<h2> ^object-handle house-2 ^anchored true ^type house ^position 2 ^left house-1 ^right house-3
           ^candidate |red| |green| |white| |yellow| |blue| |English| |Swede| |Dane| |Norwegian| |German| |tea| |coffee| |milk| |beer| |water| |PallMall| |Dunhill| |Blends| |BlueMaster| |Prince| |dogs| |birds| |cats| |horses| |zebra|)
   (<h3> ^object-handle house-3 ^anchored true ^type house ^position 3 ^left house-2 ^right house-4
           ^candidate |red| |green| |white| |yellow| |blue| |English| |Swede| |Dane| |Norwegian| |German| |tea| |coffee| |milk| |beer| |water| |PallMall| |Dunhill| |Blends| |BlueMaster| |Prince| |dogs| |birds| |cats| |horses| |zebra|)
   (<h4> ^object-handle house-4 ^anchored true ^type house ^position 4 ^left house-3 ^right house-5
           ^candidate |red| |green| |white| |yellow| |blue| |English| |Swede| |Dane| |Norwegian| |German| |tea| |coffee| |milk| |beer| |water| |PallMall| |Dunhill| |Blends| |BlueMaster| |Prince| |dogs| |birds| |cats| |horses| |zebra|)
   (<h5> ^object-handle house-5 ^anchored true ^type house ^position 5 ^left house-4
           ^candidate |red| |green| |white| |yellow| |blue| |English| |Swede| |Dane| |Norwegian| |German| |tea| |coffee| |milk| |beer| |water| |PallMall| |Dunhill| |Blends| |BlueMaster| |Prince| |dogs| |birds| |cats| |horses| |zebra|)
   (<c-color> ^object-handle category-color ^anchored true ^type category ^name color ^order 1)
   (<v-red> ^object-handle value-red ^anchored true ^type value ^name |red| ^group color)
   (<v-green> ^object-handle value-green ^anchored true ^type value ^name |green| ^group color)
   (<v-white> ^object-handle value-white ^anchored true ^type value ^name |white| ^group color)
   (<v-yellow> ^object-handle value-yellow ^anchored true ^type value ^name |yellow| ^group color)
   (<v-blue> ^object-handle value-blue ^anchored true ^type value ^name |blue| ^group color)
   (<c-nationality> ^object-handle category-nationality ^anchored true ^type category ^name nationality ^order 2)
   (<v-English> ^object-handle value-English ^anchored true ^type value ^name |English| ^group nationality ^label |Englishman|)
   (<v-Swede> ^object-handle value-Swede ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Swede| ^group nationality ^label |Swede|)
   (<v-Dane> ^object-handle value-Dane ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Dane| ^group nationality ^label |Dane|)
   (<v-Norwegian> ^object-handle value-Norwegian ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Norwegian| ^group nationality ^label |Norwegian|)
   (<v-German> ^object-handle value-German ^anchored true ^type value ^name |German| ^group nationality ^label |German|)
   (<c-drink> ^object-handle category-drink ^anchored true ^type category ^name drink ^order 3)
   (<v-tea> ^object-handle value-tea ^anchored true ^type value ^name |tea| ^group drink)
   (<v-coffee> ^object-handle value-coffee ^anchored true ^type value ^name |coffee| ^group drink)
   (<v-milk> ^object-handle value-milk ^anchored true ^type value ^name |milk| ^group drink)
   (<v-beer> ^object-handle value-beer ^anchored true ^type value ^name |beer| ^group drink)
   (<v-water> ^object-handle value-water ^anchored true ^type value ^name |water| ^group drink)
   (<c-smoke> ^object-handle category-smoke ^anchored true ^type category ^name smoke ^order 4)
   (<v-PallMall> ^object-handle value-PallMall ^anchored true ^type value ^name |PallMall| ^group smoke)
   (<v-Dunhill> ^object-handle value-Dunhill ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Dunhill| ^group smoke)
   (<v-Blends> ^object-handle value-Blends ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Blends| ^group smoke)
   (<v-BlueMaster> ^object-handle value-BlueMaster ^anchored true ^type value ^name |BlueMaster| ^group smoke)
   (<v-Prince> ^object-handle value-Prince ^anchored true ^type value ^name |Prince| ^group smoke)
   (<c-pet> ^object-handle category-pet ^anchored true ^type category ^name pet ^order 5)
   (<v-dogs> ^object-handle value-dogs ^anchored true ^type value ^name |dogs| ^group pet)
   (<v-birds> ^object-handle value-birds ^anchored true ^type value ^name |birds| ^group pet)
   (<v-cats> ^object-handle value-cats ^anchored true ^type value ^name |cats| ^group pet)
   (<v-horses> ^object-handle value-horses ^anchored true ^type value ^name |horses| ^group pet)
   (<v-zebra> ^object-handle value-zebra ^anchored true ^type value ^name |zebra| ^group pet)
   (<k2> ^object-handle clue-2 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 2 ^relation same ^x |English| ^y |red| ^text |The Englishman lives in the red house|)
   (<k3> ^object-handle clue-3 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 3 ^relation same ^x |Swede| ^y |dogs| ^text |The Swede keeps dogs|)
   (<k4> ^object-handle clue-4 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 4 ^relation same ^x |Dane| ^y |tea| ^text |The Dane drinks tea|)
   (<k5> ^object-handle clue-5 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 5 ^relation left-of ^x |green| ^y |white| ^text |The green house is immediately to the left of the white house|)
   (<k6> ^object-handle clue-6 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 6 ^relation same ^x |green| ^y |coffee| ^text |The green house owner drinks coffee|)
   (<k7> ^object-handle clue-7 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 7 ^relation same ^x |PallMall| ^y |birds| ^text |The Pall Mall smoker rears birds|)
   (<k8> ^object-handle clue-8 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 8 ^relation same ^x |yellow| ^y |Dunhill| ^text |The yellow house owner smokes Dunhill|)
   (<k9> ^object-handle clue-9 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 9 ^relation position ^x |milk| ^position 3 ^text |The man in house 3 drinks milk|)
   (<k10> ^object-handle clue-10 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 10 ^relation position ^x |Norwegian| ^position 1 ^text |The Norwegian lives in house 1|)
   (<k11> ^object-handle clue-11 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 11 ^relation next-to ^x |Blends| ^y |cats| ^text |The Blends smoker lives next to the cat keeper|)
   (<k12> ^object-handle clue-12 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 12 ^relation next-to ^x |horses| ^y |Dunhill| ^text |The horse keeper lives next to the Dunhill smoker|)
   (<k13> ^object-handle clue-13 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 13 ^relation same ^x |BlueMaster| ^y |beer| ^text |The BlueMaster smoker drinks beer|)
   (<k14> ^object-handle clue-14 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 14 ^relation same ^x |German| ^y |Prince| ^text |The German smokes Prince|)
   (<k15> ^object-handle clue-15 ^anchored true ^type clue ^number 15 ^relation next-to ^x |Norwegian| ^y |blue| ^text |The Norwegian lives next to the blue house|)
   (<ds> ^desired-count 1 ^desired <d1>)
   (<d1> ^object <d1-o>)
   (<d1-o> ^object-handle puzzle ^solved true)
   (write |Five houses; every house starts with all 25 values as candidates.| (crlf) |Deductions:| (crlf))
}

## Elaborate top state environment none: adds ^environment.
sp {zebra*elaborate*top-state*environment-none
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^name zebra)
-->
   (<s> ^environment none)
}

## Elaborate problem space: adds ^agent-world, ^default-desired-copy, ^default-operator-copy, ^default-state-copy.
sp {zebra*elaborate*problem-space
   (state <s> ^name zebra)
-->
   (<s> ^problem-space <p>)
   (<p> ^name zebra ^agent-world true ^default-state-copy no ^default-operator-copy no ^default-desired-copy no ^dont-copy top-state)
}

## Elaborate flags: adds ^flag-override, ^iterative-step, ^mea-operator-selection.
sp {zebra*elaborate*flags
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^name zebra)
-->
   (<s> ^flag-override <f>)
   (<f> ^mea-operator-selection true ^iterative-step tie-impasse)
}

## Achievement of object-property desireds (supplied by the task).
sp {zebra*elaborate*state*achieved*object-property
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^desireds <ds> ^world <w>)
   (<ds> ^desired <d>)
   (<d> ^object <do>)
   (<do> ^object-handle <h> ^{ <> object-handle <a> } <v>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects.object <ob>)
   (<ob> ^object-handle <h> ^<a> <v>)
-->
   (<ds> ^achieved <d>)
}

sp {zebra*elaborate*state*unachieved*object-property
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^desireds <ds> ^world <w>)
   (<ds> ^desired <d>)
   (<d> ^object <do>)
   (<do> ^object-handle <h> ^{ <> object-handle <a> } <v>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true)
  -{(<w> ^objects.object <ob>)
    (<ob> ^object-handle <h> ^<a> <v>)}
-->
   (<ds> ^unachieved <d>)
}

########################################################################
## The matrix: derived facts on the state (re-derived in every look-ahead copy)
########################################################################

## A house has exactly one value left in a category.
sp {zebra*elaborate*single
   (state <s> ^name zebra ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <vo>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <v>)
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <v> ^group <c>)
  -{(<h> ^candidate { <v2> <> <v> })
    (<objs> ^object <vo2>)
    (<vo2> ^type value ^name <v2> ^group <c>)}
-->
   (<s> ^single <x>)
   (<x> ^house-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^group <c> ^value <v>)
}

## A cell (house, category) not yet down to one value.
sp {zebra*elaborate*open-cell
   (state <s> ^name zebra ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <co>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p>)
   (<co> ^type category ^name <c> ^order <k>)
  -{(<s> ^single <x>)
    (<x> ^house-handle <hh> ^group <c>)}
-->
   (<s> ^open <o>)
   (<o> ^house-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^group <c> ^rank (+ (* <p> 10) <k>))
}

## The puzzle is solved when no cell holds two values of one category, no cell is empty, and no
## clue still eliminates anything (a full assignment that breaks a clue still has an elimination
## proposed, which would empty a cell).
sp {zebra*elaborate*puzzle*solved
   (state <s> ^name zebra ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <pz>)
   (<pz> ^type puzzle)
  -{(<s> ^operator <x> +)
    (<x> ^name eliminate)}
  -{(<objs> ^object <h> <a> <b>)
    (<h> ^type house ^candidate <v1> { <v2> <> <v1> })
    (<a> ^type value ^name <v1> ^group <c>)
    (<b> ^type value ^name <v2> ^group <c>)}
  -{(<objs> ^object <h2> <co>)
    (<h2> ^type house)
    (<co> ^type category ^name <c2>)
    -{(<h2> ^candidate <v3>)
      (<objs> ^object <vo3>)
      (<vo3> ^type value ^name <v3> ^group <c2>)}}
-->
   (<pz> ^solved true)
}

## Failure (a contradiction): a cell with no value left, or a value with no house left.
sp {zebra*elaborate*failure*empty-cell
   (state <s> ^name zebra ^desireds <ds> ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <co>)
   (<h> ^type house)
   (<co> ^type category ^name <c>)
  -{(<h> ^candidate <v>)
    (<objs> ^object <vo>)
    (<vo> ^type value ^name <v> ^group <c>)}
-->
   (<s> ^failure <ds>)
}

sp {zebra*elaborate*failure*value-without-house
   (state <s> ^name zebra ^desireds <ds> ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <vo>)
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <v>)
  -{(<objs> ^object <h>)
    (<h> ^type house ^candidate <v>)}
-->
   (<s> ^failure <ds>)
}

########################################################################
## eliminate: remove one candidate, for a stated reason (best and indifferent: deductions
## are taken before any branching, in any order)
########################################################################

## Propose eliminate in problem space zebra when its conditions below hold (position).
sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*position
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation position ^number <n> ^x <e> ^position <q> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position { <p> <> <q> } ^candidate <e>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |).|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*same*x
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation same ^number <n> ^x <x> ^y <e> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> -^candidate <x>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and house | <p> | cannot be | <x> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*same*y
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation same ^number <n> ^x <e> ^y <y> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> -^candidate <y>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and house | <p> | cannot be | <y> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*left-of*x
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h> <r>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation left-of ^number <n> ^x <e> ^y <y> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> ^right <rh>)
   (<r> ^object-handle <rh> -^candidate <y>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and the house to its right cannot be | <y> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*left-of*x*edge
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation left-of ^number <n> ^x <e> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> -^right)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and it has no house to its right.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*left-of*y
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h> <l>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation left-of ^number <n> ^x <x> ^y <e> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> ^left <lh>)
   (<l> ^object-handle <lh> -^candidate <x>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and the house to its left cannot be | <x> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*left-of*y*edge
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation left-of ^number <n> ^y <e> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e> -^left)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and it has no house to its left.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*next-to*x
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation next-to ^number <n> ^x <e> ^y <o> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e>)
  -{(<h> ^<< left right >> <nh>)
    (<objs> ^object <nb>)
    (<nb> ^object-handle <nh> ^candidate <o>)}
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and no neighbour of house | <p> | can be | <o> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*next-to*y
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <k> <h>)
   (<k> ^type clue ^relation next-to ^number <n> ^y <e> ^x <o> ^text <t>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <e>)
  -{(<h> ^<< left right >> <nh>)
    (<objs> ^object <nb>)
    (<nb> ^object-handle <nh> ^candidate <o>)}
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: clue | <n> | (| <t> |) and no neighbour of house | <p> | can be | <o> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*naked-single
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<s> ^single <x>)
   (<x> ^value <e> ^position <q>)
   (<objs> ^object <h>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position { <p> <> <q> } ^candidate <e>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: house | <q> | can only be | <e> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*propose*eliminate*hidden-single
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <vo> <vo2>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^candidate <v> { <e> <> <v> })
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <v> ^group <c>)
   (<vo2> ^type value ^name <e> ^group <c>)
  -{(<objs> ^object { <h2> <> <h> })
    (<h2> ^type house ^candidate <v>)}
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> + = >)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^task-operator true ^action-handle eliminate ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <e> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>
         ^reason (concat |House | <p> | is not | <e> |: only house | <p> | can be | <v> |.|) ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*apply*eliminate
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^operator <op> ^internal-actions true ^world <w>)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^pre-conditions-satisfied true ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects.object <h>)
   (<h> ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate <e>)
-->
   (<h> ^candidate <e> -)
}

## Real deductions are printed; look-ahead deductions are not.
sp {zebra*apply*eliminate*report
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^superstate nil ^operator <op> ^world <w>)
   (<op> ^name eliminate ^pre-conditions-satisfied true ^house-handle <hh> ^value <e> ^reason <r>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects.object <h>)
   (<h> ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate <e>)
-->
   (write |  | <r> (crlf))
}

########################################################################
## assign: branch on the first open cell when no deduction applies (tie -> look-ahead).
## Proposed only while no eliminate is proposed: in look-ahead the library's
## apply*operator*maintain-operator*preconditions-satisfied makes every operator best, so the
## best preference on eliminate does not hold assign back there.
########################################################################

## Propose assign in problem space zebra when its conditions below hold.
sp {zebra*propose*assign
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^flags.mea-operator-selection true ^world <w> ^desireds <ds> ^open <o>)
   (<ds> ^desired <sd> ^unachieved <sd>)
   (<o> ^house-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^group <c> ^rank <r>)
  -{(<s> ^open <o2>)
    (<o2> ^rank < <r>)}
  -{(<s> ^operator <x> +)
    (<x> ^name eliminate)}
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <vo>)
   (<h> ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate <v>)
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <v> ^group <c>)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <op> +)
   (<op> ^name assign ^task-operator true ^action-handle assign ^super-desired <sd>
         ^argument1 <v> ^argument-count 1 ^house-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^group <c> ^value <v> ^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
}

sp {zebra*apply*assign
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^operator <op> ^internal-actions true ^world <w>)
   (<op> ^name assign ^pre-conditions-satisfied true ^house-handle <hh> ^group <c> ^value <v>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <vo>)
   (<h> ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate <v> { <e> <> <v> })
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <e> ^group <c>)
-->
   (<h> ^candidate <e> -)
}

sp {zebra*apply*assign*report
   (state <s> ^problem-space.name zebra ^superstate nil ^operator <op> ^world <w>)
   (<op> ^name assign ^pre-conditions-satisfied true ^house-handle <hh> ^position <p> ^group <c> ^value <v>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects <objs>)
   (<objs> ^object <h> <vo>)
   (<h> ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate <v> { <e> <> <v> })
   (<vo> ^type value ^name <e> ^group <c>)
-->
   (write (crlf) |  Branch: house | <p> |, | <c> | = | <v> |. Look-ahead found that this choice leads to a complete solution.| (crlf))
}

########################################################################
## The elimination matrix as text (top state only), printed when deduction stalls and at the end
########################################################################

## Elaborate mark red present: adds ^house-handle, ^mark, ^text, ^value.
sp {zebra*elaborate*mark*red*present
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^name zebra ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^anchored-world true ^objects.object <h>)
   (<h> ^type house ^object-handle <hh> ^candidate |red|)
-->
   (<s> ^mark <m>)
   (<m> ^house-handle <hh> ^value |red| ^text |red |)
}

